# Compact UI controls

Default to **small** or **regular** control sizing. Do not use large buttons, inputs, or dialog chrome unless the design explicitly needs a hero CTA.

## Buttons & inputs

- Prefer `size="small"` on PrimeReact `Button`, or leave default (regular). Avoid `size="large"`.
- Prefer compact padding / `0.8–0.875rem` font for form labels and dialog body text.
- Dialog footers: small outlined Cancel + small primary action; keep button row tight.

## Confirm dialogs

- Use `confirmDialog` with a short message (1–2 sentences).
- Pass `acceptClassName` / `rejectClassName` with `p-button-sm`.
- Prefer `className: "p-confirm-dialog-sm"` (or rely on global `.pmf-compact .p-confirm-dialog` styles).
- Avoid oversized icons and multi-paragraph confirm copy.

## Nested edit dialogs

- Instruction / note editors should stay compact: modest title, hint, textarea, small footer buttons.
- Put reference-only metadata (Items, Ref, Torque) in chips **below** the input — not inside LongText / print / OARC export.
